    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the point about life planning, but isn't that just a way to rebrand the economic reality? if the end result is fewer people working and producing, doesn't that make the policy fundamentally flawed from a growth perspective? it feels like the \"support\" argument is just ignoring the actual impact on the labor market.",
